    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Vol.1 is the debut album by Angine de Poitrine, a rock-oriented release that blends prog rock, psychedelic textures, and adventurous rhythmic interplay. The record centers on driving drum grooves and intricately layered microtonal guitars, creating a hypnotic, almost ritualistic sound that draws on both experimental rock and the band’s own playful, dada-like identity.\n\nOriginally issued in 2024, Vol.1 was later re-released on CD and black vinyl by Spectacles Bonzaï, bringing the album to a wider audience after a period of self-distribution. The six-track set—featuring pieces such as “Sherpa,” “Tohogd,” and “L’Aberek”—runs just over 32 minutes and has been described as expansive yet tightly focused, with a sound that recalls Anatolian rock at its most animated while remaining distinctly eccentric and modern.",
